WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:14.530
Beyond the heavy rain is a rainbow
hageshii ame no mukou kakaru niji wo mita

3
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.170
I'll know the easy answer's a lie
tayasui kotae wa uso dato shiru darou

4
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.880
Vow not to back down to the shouting
dekai koe nanka ni makenai to chikatte

5
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.630
I need you alone to understand tomorrow
anata hitori ni wakatte hoshii ashita

6
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.770
You gave me the time of my life
yume no youna jikan kureta anata

7
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:51.280
What do I look like? An ANGEL or a DEVIL...
watashi wa dou mieteruno? sorega tenshi ka akuma ka

8
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:56.240
Beyond the dawn, beyond the dawn
yoake no mukou yoake no mukou

9
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.740
There's so much I want to tell you
hanashitai koto takusan arun da

10
00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.540
Filled with love, with love
ai kometa ai kometa

11
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.460
That can't be written down in a letter
tegami ni kakikirenai omoi da

12
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:20.890
A small hand in search of eternity
eien wo sagashita chiisana tenohira

13
00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:39.160
<b>"A Fleeting Moment of Happiness -
Kumachi and Ginny"</b>

14
00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:47.540
<b>Sorbet Kingdom, 
South Blue</b>

15
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.490
Going back 30 years ago.

16
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.540
This is the Sorbet Kingdom
in the South Blue.

17
00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:52.500
Eight years after the God Valley Incident.

18
00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.130
Heave ho...

19
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.300
Help me, Kumachi.

20
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:02.760
You got it.

21
00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.070
I feel much better.

22
00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:14.400
Thank you.

23
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.110
Who's next?

24
00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.700
Me.

25
00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.490
My back hurts and I can't sleep well.

26
00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.910
Help me again.

27
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.670
You've always been a great help, Kumachi.

28
00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.550
I've been attending this church
since your father's time.

29
00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.460
So I was surprised
when all of you suddenly disappeared...

30
00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:41.300
We were relieved when you came back.

31
00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.010
I'm sure your parents are happy somewhere,

32
00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.440
knowing that their son
has become a great pastor.

33
00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.850
<b>Bartholomew Kuma 
(Age 17), Pastor</b>

34
00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.310
The pain is gone!

35
00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.650
Thank you so much.

36
00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.280
What a blessing.

37
00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.410
He'll remove any kind of pain...

38
00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.990
They're indeed Miracle Hands.

39
00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:08.000
Hey, Kumachi.
Can't you do this on weekdays, too?

40
00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.920
No! Just Sundays!

41
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:21.590
You don't even pay for this.
You're so shameless, you old codgers!

42
00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.350
Here comes the mean Ginny!

43
00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.310
Oh, shut up!

44
00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:30.480
This is not a campground or a hospital!

45
00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.060
Go away!

46
00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.650
She has such a foul mouth,
but since she's so pretty...

47
00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:44.660
<b>Ginny (Age 21)</b>

48
00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:44.530
Men from the town
never stop asking her out!

49
00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.370
Don't change the subject!

50
00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.580
Well, she's already got Kumachi.

51
00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.580
What?

52
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.830
Oh, I think we nailed it.

53
00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.090
You can't deceive us.

54
00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.500
We're not living longer for nothing.

55
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.300
That's enough!

56
00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.010
If you're done here, go home already!

57
00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.390
Don't be so mean, Ginny.

58
00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.970
Seeing Kumachi's face helps us relax.

59
00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.310
Glad to hear that.

60
00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.600
You're being too sweet to them!

61
00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:24.280
I'd pay Kumachi as much as I could...

62
00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:31.370
But it's already hard enough to get by
because of the Heavenly Tribute...

63
00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.080
And now we've got this new king.

64
00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:40.800
King Bekori is famously
cold and heartless.

65
00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:45.050
If we fall ill,
we can't pay the Heavenly Tribute...

66
00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.850
And then he'll lock us up!

67
00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.470
How terrible.

68
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.770
I heard that an old man who was jailed
the other day starved to death.

69
00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:54.770
Starved!

70
00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:58.770
The king won't even feed prisoners.
What a skinflint.

71
00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:04.030
But he sucks up to the Celestial Dragons.
He's really despicable.

72
00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:07.280
Old people who are poor can't survive.

73
00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.660
We have to be healthy, or we'll die.

74
00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.670
If it's a minor ailment or pain,
I can take it away for you.

75
00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:18.960
Come every week.

76
00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.340
- Are you sure?
- We appreciate it, Kumachi.

77
00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.390
This is all we can give you...

78
00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:39.060
Eat it with Ginny later.

79
00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.110
Thank you!

80
00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:43.980
Goodbye!

81
00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.780
Please help us again!

82
00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.950
Yeah, see you next week!

83
00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.200
How can you do this to yourself
every week?

84
00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.960
They don't even know
that you're suffering.

85
00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.250
There's no other choice...

86
00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.920
The mass of pain and suffering...

87
00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:30.510
...won't just disappear
until someone accepts it.

88
00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:35.010
If left untouched,
it'd return to the person it came from.

89
00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.140
Most importantly, I feel delighted...

90
00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.190
...to see everyone happy.

91
00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.940
I'm sorry for worrying you.

92
00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:53.280
I'll train harder and become stronger...

93
00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.740
That's not the issue.

94
00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:58.330
I'm okay now.

95
00:07:58.790 --> 00:07:59.870
You sure?

96
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.620
They gave us some food, right?
Let's eat.

97
00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.540
Yay! Mealtime!

98
00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.260
Let's eat!

99
00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:12.880
Let's eat.

100
00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.060
Yummy!

101
00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.060
Hey, Ginny.

102
00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:27.650
If it's sunny tomorrow,
can we go somewhere?

103
00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:31.570
Sounds good! How about a barbecue?

104
00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.780
It's right around the time
for the salmon run,

105
00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.700
so maybe by the river?

106
00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.990
Yeah. Let's do that.

107
00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.830
Ya-hoo! Can't wait!

108
00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:49.130
<b>25 Years Ago</b>

109
00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:49.130
Time rolled on, but when Kuma was 22...

110
00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.550
Thank you as always.

111
00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.070
Good morning, Kumachi.

112
00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.360
Good morning, Ginny.

113
00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.780
Do you want me to make some coffee?

114
00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.030
Yeah.

115
00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.740
I love the coffee you make!

116
00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.870
It'll be ready soon.

117
00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.260
I've got an idea!

118
00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.600
Let's get married, Kumachi!

119
00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:48.810
What?!

120
00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:03.490
No!

121
00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:04.870
What?!

122
00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.290
Why?! Let's just get married!

123
00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.340
I know you really love me!

124
00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.880
I promise I'll make you happy!

125
00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:18.840
I know I'll be happy, but...

126
00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.970
I'm the only one who has Buccaneer blood!

127
00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.270
My wife doesn't!

128
00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.850
Let her and my boy go!

129
00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:33.020
Your mother's dead...

130
00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:36.030
Please understand, Ginny.

131
00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.660
I don't want to bring you misery.

132
00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.330
Kumachi!

133
00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.540
L-Look!

134
00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.920
Another article about the Freedom Fighters.

135
00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:56.250
They've incited protests
in various countries

136
00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.300
and have been placed on the wanted list!

137
00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:01.970
Dragon. He's so cool.

138
00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:05.140
I'm sure he's thought of as a hero.

139
00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:09.850
I want to go out to the sea someday
and devote my life...

140
00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.100
...to saving others, too.

141
00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:15.570
Just like Nika, the Warrior of Liberation.

142
00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.530
Hey! Are you here?!

143
00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:25.990
Who is it?
It's still early in the morning.

144
00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.000
Hi, Kuma!

145
00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.540
Sorry to bother you this early.

146
00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:36.880
What's up?

147
00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:44.390
It's the lovely Ginny!

148
00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:47.720
We caught a huge haul today.
Please take some fish!

149
00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:50.600
Oh! Thanks, Gyogyo!

150
00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:55.020
Ouch!

151
00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:56.770
She's mad at you.

152
00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:07.700
Dummy.

153
00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.760
And then 22 years ago,

154
00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:29.390
a major incident took place
in the Sorbet Kingdom.

155
00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.560
<b>Royal City, 
Sorbet Kingdom</b>

156
00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:34.560
Wait!

157
00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:40.110
<b>Kuma 
(Age 25)</b>

158
00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.060
What are you doing?!

159
00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:40.110
Release those you kidnapped!

160
00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:42.940
Who is this big loser?

161
00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.320
He's a pastor from the South.

162
00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.330
You're just a pastor, stay out of this!

163
00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.490
Are you trying to defy the Royal Army?!

164
00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.750
Kumachi, help!

165
00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.170
Don't move, old bag!

166
00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:03.590
Hey, Father!

167
00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.720
I'm sure you heard
that the laws have changed.

168
00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:12.520
Now we're free to use people from the South
however we want.

169
00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.850
You're turning them into slaves?!

170
00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.770
Stop it right now!

171
00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:21.820
K-Kumachi!

172
00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:26.490
It's His Majesty's policy.

173
00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.780
We'll drive them to work hard.

174
00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.530
Until they die.

175
00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.830
Stop!

176
00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:41.380
Damn you!

177
00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.880
You crossed the line!

178
00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.270
You rebels!

179
00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.360
Enslaving you isn't enough!

180
00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.070
I'm gonna kill you!

181
00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.620
What's that?!

182
00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:21.000
It's an unforgivable sin!

183
00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.260
Your Majesty.

184
00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:37.980
This policy is not well received
among the people of the kingdom.

185
00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:39.690
Won't the people resist?

186
00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:42.860
Don't worry.

187
00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:46.440
People tend to be easily swayed by labels.

188
00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:49.990
Soon, they'll start looking down on the South.

189
00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:50.820
Right...

190
00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:55.290
Starting today, only the north part of the island is the Sorbet Kingdom.

191
00:14:56.660 --> 00:15:00.290
The amount of the Heavenly Tribute
to be paid to the Government...

192
00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.420
...is determined
by the number of citizens.

193
00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:07.670
Thus, the South, with its many old people
who can't pay much Heavenly Tribute,

194
00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:08.840
<b>Kuma's Church</b>

195
00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:10.090
<b>Sorbet Kingdom</b>

196
00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.840
<b>Elderly Village</b>

197
00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.840
<b>Lawless Area</b>

198
00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:10.550
<b>Castle and Royal City</b>

199
00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:08.840
is dragging us down.

200
00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:13.600
If we cut them off,
this kingdom will become rich.

201
00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:13.600
<b>Kuma's Church</b>

202
00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.600
<b>Elderly Village</b>

203
00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:13.600
<b>Lawless Area</b>

204
00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:16.970
It's that easy...

205
00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:19.640
<b>Prison</b>

206
00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:38.370
Why are you guys in here, too?

207
00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.750
We ran amok,
saying we wanted you back...

208
00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.050
They beat the hell out of us.

209
00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.180
We did something out of character...

210
00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:53.760
But it felt good.

211
00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.310
This is wrong...

212
00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:03.350
Just because you're living in the South,
you'll be enslaved...

213
00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:05.310
Kumachi...

214
00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:14.280
Ginny. This country is turning into a place
 where the poor suffer harsh discrimination.

215
00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.370
King Bekori is the Celestial Dragons' puppet.

216
00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:20.620
This policy was put in his head from above.

217
00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:23.040
If we want to rebel against this country,

218
00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.170
we must be determined
to fight the World Government.

219
00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:40.560
Who are you people?!

220
00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.360
Your Majesty! Please evacuate!

221
00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:00.870
I won't let you escape.
You stupid Celestial Dragon wannabe!

222
00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:02.290
How sickening!

223
00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.540
D-Don't tell me you're...

224
00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.080
Thanks to outside intervention,

225
00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:12.210
the Sorbet Kingdom narrowly avoided
that evil policy.

226
00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.630
The king has given in!

227
00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.930
The slave policy is repealed!

228
00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:20.390
Thank goodness!
I don't wanna live in such a country.

229
00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:26.560
Seems like your favorite guy
really created a scene.

230
00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:30.020
I'm sure you'll like him at first sight,
Dragon.

231
00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.870
Kuma! Ginny! You guys were caught!

232
00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.830
I'm here to get you out!

233
00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:48.040
What?! Iva-chan?!

234
00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.500
Big Bro?!

235
00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:52.840
And that man you're with...

236
00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:00.010
Dragon?!

237
00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:05.430
Hey, Kuma!

238
00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.980
If you're still the same man
you were then,

239
00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:12.360
join us to change the world together!

240
00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:20.820
Okay!

241
00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.160
I'm going, too!

242
00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.620
Heehaw!

243
00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:33.170
The Freedom Fighters, who transformed
people's anger at governments into protests,

244
00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:36.170
decided to take up arms...

245
00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:40.680
...in response to the advent of the Pirate Era
and the tragedy of Ohara.

246
00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:45.560
Adding Kuma to their twin pillars of
Dragon and Ivankov,

247
00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.230
they transformed themselves
into the Revolutionary Army,

248
00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:51.190
which would become infamous
throughout the world.

249
00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:56.820
We still don't have enough money.

250
00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:01.870
Like mercenaries, we'll help those
who aspire to rebel to overthrow their kings.

251
00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:06.950
Those who wish to join will be taught
 how to use weapons and fight with them.

252
00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:11.000
Eventually, I want it to be a huge army
spread across the world.

253
00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.880
When did you learn how to
 use weapons, Dragon?

254
00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.670
I spent a short time in the Marines.

255
00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:21.510
Unfortunately,
I couldn't find any "justice" there.

256
00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:23.970
Both the Marines
and the Revolutionary Army...

257
00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:28.180
...just want to help people.

258
00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:32.150
I'm with you to the end, Dragon.

259
00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:33.860
Me too!

260
00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.900
You won't regret it.

261
00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:57.670
Oh! You returned, Kumachi!

262
00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.510
I was worried about you all.

263
00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:04.340
I'll be back to see you from time to time.

264
00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.800
How sweet.

265
00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:10.060
Is anybody sick or hurt?

266
00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.440
And eight more years passed.

267
00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.520
14 years ago, in a certain kingdom...

268
00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:22.570
<b>Revolutionary Army Captain,
 Eastern Forces, Ginny</b>

269
00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:23.240
Kumachi! Kumachi!

270
00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:27.780
You look happy, Ginny-san.

271
00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:29.910
Oh, is it showing?

272
00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.410
Because tomorrow...

273
00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.130
...we'll meet up with Kumachi's group.

274
00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.710
I really can't wait!

275
00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.630
I wish I were Captain Kuma.

276
00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.680
He's loved by everyone's crush.

277
00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:47.470
What? You've got a crush on me?!

278
00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:49.560
Ew! You snotty brats!

279
00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:50.970
So harsh.

280
00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:55.810
<b>Baltigo, Revolutionary 
Army Headquarters</b>

281
00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.810
Dragon-san! Dragon-san!

282
00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.400
Ginny's been...

283
00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.280
...abducted?!

284
00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:03.320
I'm sorry!
The enemy caught us off guard...

285
00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:37.020
I can't protect anyone again
mata daremo mamorenai no

286
00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:41.820
It's my fault that the voice is fading away
kiekakaru koe wa boku no sei

287
00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:44.110
I don't even have time to look down
utsumuku hima mo nai no

288
00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.700
Gravel marks on my palms
tenohira ni tsuku jari no ato

289
00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:50.080
Start moving again, my ship
mata ugokidase boku no fune yo

290
00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:55.580
Though I can't fly in the broad sky
hiroi sora wa tobenai kedo

291
00:21:55.580 --> 00:22:01.460
I can light up the deep sea
fukai umi wa teraseru kara

292
00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.420
We
bokura wa

293
00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:04.920
EVERYDAY owarenai
EVERYDAY, can't let this be the end

294
00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:07.550
EVERYDAY makerenai
EVERYDAY, can't be defeated

295
00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:11.310
We have something here to protect
mamoru mono ga koko niwa aru

296
00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:13.850
This may not be what I expected
yosou chigai kamo?

297
00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.560
But we can't stop now
tomarenai yo mou

298
00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:21.860
We go on, sharing loneliness
kodoku wo ima wakeai susumu

299
00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:24.610
Don't be afraid
ojikedzukuna yo

300
00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:28.570
I'm not the same person I was that day
ano hi no boku to chigau kara

301
00:22:28.610 --> 00:22:32.030
No one can stand in my way
dare nimo jama dekinai yo

302
00:22:32.790 --> 00:22:33.660
Now, move aside
saa doite

303
00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:36.250
Conquer the world, believe in the future
sekai wo seishite mirai wo shinjite

304
00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:38.830
Count up the nights
ikutsu mono yoru kazoete

305
00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:41.540
What did you see? What did you learn?
nani wo mite nani wo shitte

306
00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:44.550
To realize what was important
taisetsu na koto ni kidzuita no
